   "fix": "State the implemented rule: \"its mathlib is an ancestor of M, or it has diverged from M and M is a release tag on that line\"; add that a dependency commit whose manifest pins no mathlib fits on the toolchain line alone. Fix both scripts/resolve_deps.py:41-42 and docs/dependency-bumps.md:46-47.",
   "issue": "The documented `near` rule (\"its mathlib is an ancestor of M, or M is a release tag on that line\") is weaker than `fit`: the code only accepts the tag case when the dependency's mathlib has *diverged* from M, so a dependency pinning a mathlib that is a descendant of M (compare status `behind`) on the same Lean line is reported as no fit although the docs predict one \u2014 reachable whenever M is an rc tag on master and the dependency has moved past it, which is TauCeti's shape in the recorded fixture. The docs also omit the `commit[\"mathlib\"] is None` branch, which returns `near` on the toolchain line alone. Same wording in docs/dependency-bumps.md:46-47.",
